From f74ebf16b5b96658221b059344d414e2a094eef2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lyuweiwang <lwfvx@missouri.edu>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 22:58:13 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Template parsing fixes and confidence-module memory
 reductions for PLABench

PLABench benchmark patches on top of upstream 832486d (the commit the
benchmark environment was installed from):
- data/parse/mmcif.py: walk the alignment string with a separate sequence
  index so gaps ('-') and mismatches ('.') no longer shift residue indices.
- data/parse/schema.py: template chains without a sequence (ligand chains)
  score 0 / are skipped instead of raising KeyError; template matching sees
  every chain, not only protein chains.
- model/layers/pairformer.py, model/modules/trunkv2.py: optional chunked
  z-transition, enabled only for the confidence stack.
- model/modules/confidencev2.py: accumulate the pair conditioning terms in
  place, skip the no-op repeat_interleave when multiplicity == 1, and free
  the distogram embedding early. Numerically identical; keeps ~3300-token
  complexes under 80 GB.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
